<title>UK: Credit Local sets 300 million mark four-year bond. [CORRECTED 11:05 GMT]</title>
<headline>Credit Local sets 300 million mark four-year bond. [CORRECTED 11:05 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Societe Generale and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CREDIT LOCAL DE FRANCE</p>
<p> AMT    300 MLN DEM   COUPON     4.375     MATURITY    23.JUL.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.878   PAY DATE    23.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.15	REOFFER    99.953    SPREAD	+12 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	  LISTING    FFT/LUX   PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p>(CORRECTS MOODY RATING FROM A2)  S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMS US/GB/FR/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.525     LISTING FEE 0.40</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND BOBL 119 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
